# Kong runs DB-less with a declarative config. That is one of Kong's two documented deployment
# modes and not its default, which is Postgres-backed; the default is not usable here because it
# would put a database on the box we are measuring, sharing the cores and the disk with the gateway
# under test. Every setting below is needed to boot the process or to bind the port the rig drives.
KONG_DATABASE=off
KONG_DECLARATIVE_CONFIG=/kong/kong.yml
KONG_PROXY_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:{GW_PORT}
# nginx's `auto` reads the HOST's online CPU count and is blind to the cpuset, so without this the
# gateway would run sixteen workers on the four cores it was pinned to.
KONG_NGINX_WORKER_PROCESSES={NCORE}
